# FORLORN HOPE: the whole game, played from the title by the demo player with
# real button presses: 28 volunteers, one after another, each with its own
# plan. A mason stones the spike pit, the next takes key 1 and stones plate
# 1; a runner climbs the Old Yew and leaves a waystone by plate 2, which a
# mason stones; a sapper opens the loose rock; a runner goes over the
# bridge and up the steps the plates raised and leaves a waystone by the
# gulper; a mason stones plate 3 and a sapper feeds the gulper. Hunters
# and sappers wear the stingback down in the deep (its wounds persist), a
# hunter climbs the tower and shoots the hornet bell, four masons cap the
# tower's drains, a runner leaves a waystone at the top, three sappers blow
# the seal open, and eight sappers burst the four thorn hearts. It wins
# having lost fewer than 50, so all three goals light up.
game forlorn
wait 20
botuntil state == 3 400
botuntil switches >= 1 2000
expect goals == 1
botuntil plate1 == 1 3000
botuntil plate2 == 1 3000
expect first_on17 == 1
botuntil first_on17 == 0 2000
botuntil first_on16 == 0 8000
botuntil stones >= 8 12000
botuntil hearts <= 3 12000
botuntil state == 5 12000
expect hearts == 0
expect lost == 28
expect lost < 50
expect lives == 72
expect goals == 7
expect wins == 1
expect best_lost == 28
expect bot_stuck == 0
